# q6_measure
Task 6, stage 5  measured storage tiers of this machine
probe file: tmp/q6_probe.bin, 1024 MB

random 4 KB reads  : 5000 reads
  mean       7.0 us   p50      4.6 us   p95     18.1 us   p99     32.1 us
  142164 random IOPS (single thread)

sequential read    : 512 MB in 216.2 ms = 2483.2 MB/s
sequential write   : 256 MB in 878.7 ms = 305.5 MB/s (with fsync)

note: the probe file was just written, so the operating system
cache answers part of the reads: p50 is a cache hit, p99 is closer to
the device.  The simulator therefore uses a conservative 0.25 ms
for an SSD read instead of the 7.0 us cache hit measured here.
